mintcam (0.2.7) noble; urgency=medium

  * The header logo now loads a PNG first. It used to look for the JPEG only,
    and Qt needs a separate image format plugin for JPEG, which Debian keeps
    in its own package: without it QPixmap could not decode the logo and the
    header showed a placeholder glyph. PNG support is built into Qt.
  * Remove the Flatpak packaging. It was submitted to Flathub, was never
    accepted, and its manifest had drifted from the application: it still
    installed PySide6 while the app now uses PyQt6, so anyone building it
    would have gotten a broken application. No Flatpak of MintCam is
    distributed anywhere.
  * README: drop the Flatpak mentions from the changelog and say explicitly
    that no Flatpak is distributed.

 -- Alex Mirici <hilliedmikerano@gmail.com>  Mon, 12 Oct 2026 20:50:00 +0200

